ay trusts that record without re-validating successor state or reading history; it joins recorded and drafted successors in one lineage operation, and refuses a request without a record, a record without a request, unequal request and record, a malformed record, or an unreadable merged specification. Every line whose text begins with a fence marker is a fence line; a disposition fence stands at column zero, opens only as TOML and closes only as a bare paired fence.\""," rationale = \"Validating at the close fixes the successor relation at the event that records it, while a durable record lets later replay preserve that relation without treating later successor state or unavailable history as authority.\""," test_refs = \"TC-360\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3566,"oldLines":6,"newStart":3566,"newLines":6,"lines":[" detail = \"A commit that changes an adoption record or moves a requesting specification into docs/work/complete or docs/archive/work/complete is admitted only when it is the close's own commit or carries an existing record with its request unchanged in some parent. A merge is judged only on the changes absent from every parent, under that same rule. The close's own commit has one readable parent, paired moves from one docs/work/active branch to docs/work/complete, no created or destroyed path outside those moves, the composed close subject, and each changed path outside docs/work exactly the inbound relink written by those moves as determined by the shared byte-exact relink reading; its record equals its request and every adopted id is valid in the parent tree. The tree under judgement is read strictly; a parent's specification whose front matter or record does not parse holds no record, while a parent git cannot read is refused and named. Every other record change, a carried record whose request changed or was removed, or a requesting move without a record is refused. The rule applies to the lane-commit walk and staged commit check, including their squash handling.\""," rationale = \"The close record is authority only when its creating commit proves it was the validated result of a machinery close; unchanged carriage and merges preserve that authority without admitting a second writer.\""," test_refs = \"TC-383\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-969\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3776,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3776,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"A disposition adoption resolves an already-open superseding successor once at close, records that result, and later replays only the recorded result while refusing every declared malformed or incomplete request-and-record pair.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_an_adoption_block_is_parsed_apart_from_the_drafts; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_a_malformed_adoption_block_is_a_parse_refusal; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_the_disposed_row_is_read_from_either_minted_title_form; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_acceptance_is_read_against_the_registry_with_distinct_refusals; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_a_repeated_adoption_is_a_parse_refusal; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_a_valid_block_then_an_unclosed_one_is_refused; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_a_fence_that_is_not_toml_or_a_bare_close_is_refused; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_every_dispositions_section_in_the_repository_passes_the_fence_grammar; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_an_adoption_never_counts_as_an_absorption; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_an_adopted_cell_survives_the_spec_row_reader; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_the_record_reader_accepts_only_a_list_of_distinct_ids; tests/test_disposition_adoption.py::test_the_record_change_table; tests/test_handback.py::test_an